# ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │  KubeNova — environment configuration                                   │
# │                                                                         │
# │  Quick start (2 steps):                                                 │
# │    1. cp .env.example .env                                              │
# │    2. ./start.sh          (or: docker compose up)                       │
# │                                                                         │
# │  Default uses Ollama (free, no API key) running inside Docker.          │
# │  First start downloads the model (~2 GB). Subsequent starts are fast.   │
# └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

# ── LLM Provider ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Choose ONE block below. Comment out the others.

# ── Option A: Ollama (free, no API key — default) ────────────────────────────
# Runs entirely inside Docker. Pulls the model automatically on first start.
# Tip (Apple Silicon): native Ollama is faster — install with:
#   brew install ollama && brew services start ollama
#   then set LLM_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434 and COMPOSE_PROFILES=
COMPOSE_PROFILES=ollama
LLM_PROVIDER=ollama
LLM_MODEL=llama3.2
LLM_API_KEY=
LLM_BASE_URL=http://ollama:11434

# ── Option B: Anthropic Claude ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Get a key at https://console.anthropic.com (requires $5 credit minimum).
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=
# LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
# LLM_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001
# LLM_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# LLM_BASE_URL=

# ── Option C: Google Gemini ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Get a free key at https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=
# LLM_PROVIDER=openai
# LLM_MODEL=gemini-2.0-flash
# LLM_API_KEY=<google-ai-studio-key>
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/

# ── Kubernetes ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# KubeNova auto-mounts your ~/.kube directory into the backend container.
# Point it at any cluster (EKS, GKE, AKS, k3d, minikube, etc.).
# If no kubeconfig exists, the app starts with "no cluster connected" state.
#
# Override the kubeconfig directory (optional):
# KUBECONFIG_DIR=/custom/path/.kube

# ── Application ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
KUBENOVA_ENV=development
KUBENOVA_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
